.DS_Store

# Attention-visualization output. ~190 MB of PNG triples (_attention,
# _original, _overlay) for ~105 observations, of which two appear in
# Figure 1. The _original files are iNaturalist contributors' photographs,
# whose licenses vary per observation, so these are deliberately not
# distributed from this repository, and are not deposited elsewhere. The
# fitted model they were generated from was not retained, so they cannot be
# regenerated without retraining; the two panels used in Figure 1 are
# published in the figure itself.
results/attention_results/

# R
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
renv/library/
renv/staging/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db

# Illustrator sources for the multi-panel figures. They live here so that the
# panels they link to, the composites they export, and the code that makes the
# panels are all in one place -- but they are not tracked. They are large
# opaque binaries (~177 MB), and git stores a whole new copy on every save.
figures/*.ai
figures/**/*.ai

# Per-image prediction log. 5.7 MB of intermediate output; results/all_predictions.json
# is the version the analyses read.
results/predictions_log.json

# Figure panels. Regenerated by the analysis scripts (seasonal_panels.R,
# seasonal_tiles.R, norm.R, seasonal_histograms.R, model_figures.R) and
# assembled into the composites in figures/ via Illustrator. Rebuildable in one
# command, so the panels themselves are not tracked.
figures/panels/

# The two Figure 1 attention panels and their source photographs, currently
# linked from image_classification.ai in place. Panels are not tracked (see
# above), and unlike the rest of figures/panels/ these cannot be rebuilt --
# the fitted model was not retained. The photographs are CC BY and credited
# in the figure caption, which is where they are published.
machine_learning/*.png

# Review copies of the rendered manuscript. These are circulated, not tracked:
# the repository is already dominated by PDF blobs and each copy is ~33 MB.
manuscript/*REVIEW*.pdf
